# {{ artifact.name }}

An optional speed add-on for [{{ overlay.thor_repo }}](https://huggingface.co/{{ overlay.thor_repo }}). It holds NVFP4 copies of that build's dense FP8 linear weights ({{ overlay.layers }} layers, {{ overlay.bytes_gib }} GiB; `overlay.json` lists them). The CUDA decoder uses them in place of the FP8 originals when single-token decode is bound by memory traffic. The routed experts and everything else are unchanged; this repo is useless without the Thor build.

## What it costs and what it buys

Both numbers come from the build pipeline, never typed by hand.

| | Thor build | Thor build + overlay |
|---|---|---|
| decode tok/s, short context | {{ overlay.tok_base }} | {{ overlay.tok_ovl }} |
| decode tok/s, after an 8k-token prompt | {{ overlay.tok8k_base }} | {{ overlay.tok8k_ovl }} |
| top-1 agreement with the unpruned model | {{ overlay.top1_base }} | {{ overlay.top1_ovl }} |

Paired against the same build without the overlay on the held-out confirmation split, kl32 changes by {{ overlay.d_kl32 }} and confident-token flips by {{ overlay.flips }} percentage points. Both are within the pre-registered overlay gate (`ops/s10_gates.json` "overlay"). Speeds are greedy, batch 1, Engram rows on NVMe, measured by the s08 decode gate on the `{{ overlay.build }}` build with and without this overlay.

## How to use it

Download this repository next to the Thor build and start the server with the overlay directory in the environment:

```
DSV4_NVFP4_OVERLAY=<this repo> v41_server --ckpt <thor build> --keepset <thor build>/reap_keepset.json --engram <row-file dir> --port 18108
```

Without the variable, nothing from this repo is loaded and the decoder runs the FP8 path unchanged.

